# written by the harness, not by hand, and they are the proof that a rules change
# replays byte-identically. Prettier reflowed all nine on 12/09/2026: the DATA
# survived (fixtures.test.ts parses rather than byte-compares, so nothing broke)
# but a regenerate would have fought the reformat every time.
packages/sim/fixtures/

# The dashboard template (2026-09-20). Its payload injection marker is an EXACT
# string, `/*__DATA__*/null`, which tools/sim-dashboard.py finds with a literal
# str.replace. Prettier rewrites it to `/*__DATA__*/ null`, the replace then
# never matches, and the tool writes a byte-copy of the template while still
# printing "warnings 0" and "wrote ...". A dashboard that silently contains no
# data is worse than one that fails, so this file is never auto-formatted.
tools/sim-dashboard-template.html
